              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.141
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Label the plants in your school with their local names with the help of your teacher or the gardener. List them in your notebook."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.147,
            0.884,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " With the help of your teacher, plan a field visit or a nature walk. Record your observations. Prepare a class biodiversity register by consolidating the observations and notes of all the students taken during the field visit or nature walk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.229,
            0.883,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find out about ‘Project Tiger’ and other similar projects initiated in India to protect our biodiversity. Prepare a presentation for your class."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.292,
            0.883,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Divide your class into groups of six students each. Initiate a discussion in the class on how you can protect biodiversity around you. Prepare a group-wise report that includes suggestions given by members of each group."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.374,
            0.884,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Interact with elders in your family or neighbourhood to find out various plants and animals that they see now but were not seen earlier and vice-versa. Collect pictures of these plants and animals and paste them in a scrapbook. Find out more about them from your teacher."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.892,
            0.111,
            0.908
          ],
